 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? You' using a web camera, right? If so, it' likely the quality is being limited by that. A good dedicated camera would improve it a lot. Then shoot in a room with big windows and turn on the desk light as well as the room light. Use a tripod for the camera so it's as steady as possible. Try to talk as clearly as possible and see if you can open a window for fresh air. A little background music can help too, something not too loud. Shoot directly at the other person if you can, or at least level with them if you shooting over something. A strong flash can help too, just make sure it' not in their eyes.",
